# Pairs with SetSagaConsistent (the requested InFlightRecheckSkipped). The set
# capture skips the in-flight re-check under the gate AND does not validate
# the registration epoch. Skipping either alone is safe in this design, and
# is measured clean: a delegation row can be live at the gate only if a lease
# lapse let a registration in after the drain, and that registration also
# moves the epoch the drain recorded. The two checks back each other up; only
# losing both admits a set that is torn across its members.
MODULE: SetSagaConsistentRecheckAndEpochSkipped
TARGET: SetSagaConsistent
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the gated in-flight re-check and the epoch validation are both skipped
PERTURBS: Recheck, Validate

--- FIND
    /\ IF kind = "single" \/ \A T \in Members : ~InFlight(T)
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: no re-check.
    /\ IF TRUE
--- END

--- FIND
          /\ kind = "set" => \A T \in Members : epoch[T] = before[T]
--- REPLACE
          \* MUTATION: no epoch validation.
          /\ TRUE
--- END
